---
name: implementation-delivery
description: Use by default for every non-trivial code-changing task, including features, bug fixes, refactors, migrations, UI work, and security changes. Coordinate the work from plan through cherry-pickable pushed commits, verification, screenshots, E2E and adversarial coverage, documentation, handoff, and a review-ready outcome. Skip read-only analysis and trivial edits.
---

# Implementation delivery

Own an authorized implementation through its requested endpoint. Use specialist
skills for their domains; this skill coordinates them and defines completion.

## Plan and route

1. Read repository instructions, inspect the working tree, and identify existing
   conventions before proposing changes.
2. Turn the request into coherent, independently reviewable slices. Separate:
   - dependent work that must run in order;
   - user-only or approval-gated actions;
   - independent, long-running checks that can run concurrently or in the
     background without hiding failures.
3. Discover the skills relevant to the actual work, then load the smallest set
   that materially changes execution. For every non-trivial UI change, consult
   the applicable design-system and platform-design skills before editing.
4. Ask before introducing either:
   - a UI concept without a clear precedent in the codebase; or
   - a new dependency. Show the closest existing code and a concrete proposed
     snippet. For a dependency, explain why existing primitives or a small local
     implementation are insufficient, including maintenance and bundle/runtime
     tradeoffs.

Do not stop merely to announce next steps. Continue through the plan until the
requested outcome is complete or an unexpected blocker requires user input or
new authority.

## Implement in reviewable slices

- Reuse current architecture, UI primitives, and test infrastructure. Keep each
  commit coherent enough to review, revert, and cherry-pick independently;
  avoid checkpoint commits that leave the branch knowingly broken.
- Commit each completed notable slice and, when the user has authorized remote
  publication, push it promptly so the remote branch is a durable handoff.
- Prefer rebasing the feature branch onto its confirmed base and fast-forwarding
  integration when the user requests a linear history. Never rewrite shared
  history or choose an integration method without authority; use the dedicated
  Git integration skill for the operation.
- For dismissible modals, verify backdrop/outside press closes them. Do not add
  outside-press dismissal to destructive confirmations, mandatory decisions, or
  platform patterns where accidental dismissal would lose work.
- When multiple user-visible Codex tasks are explicitly created, prefix the
  coordinating task title with `orchestrator:` when title control is available.

## Verify every slice

- Add permanent automated coverage for each feature at the lowest layer that
  proves its behavior. User-visible flows should also receive E2E coverage when
  the repository can run them reliably; record a justified gap when external
  infrastructure makes that impossible.
- Reuse existing E2E routes to reach changed screens cheaply. Promote useful
  development-time Argent, Maestro, or equivalent flows into deterministic,
  redacted or mocked regression tests when practical. Never store production
  secrets or unredacted personal data in fixtures.
- For security behavior, add adversarial tests that exercise unauthorized,
  malformed, replayed, boundary, and direct-query attempts appropriate to the
  threat model.
- For each UI-changing commit, capture review evidence for every shipped target
  affected by the change. Associate screenshots with the commit SHA in the PR,
  handoff, or artifact store; do not commit diagnostic images unless repository
  policy asks for them.
- Finish with the repository's full relevant unit, integration, E2E, device,
  lint, type, build, and CI checks. A command passing is not enough: confirm the
  documented setup works from its stated prerequisites and that the test
  actually exercised the intended behavior.

Delegate bounded independent checks only when delegation is available and
useful. Give each worker exact setup, ownership, commands, and acceptance
criteria; keep device assignments distinct from other active work. The
coordinator reviews reported failures, fixes code or documentation, and reruns
the affected gate. Do not delegate every command by default or use delegation
to evade approvals.

## Documentation and continuity

- Keep the repository's handoff document current during long work and at every
  pushed milestone. If none exists and continuity risk is real, create the
  repository-standard handoff file. Record branch/base/HEAD SHAs, completed and
  pending slices, exact commands, environment prerequisites, evidence paths,
  blockers, and the next executable action.
- Update user and contributor documentation whenever behavior, setup, commands,
  environment variables, data models, or operational procedures change. Write
  commands so a new contributor or less-capable agent can execute them without
  unstated local knowledge; use placeholders for secrets.
- Simplify the final branch and remove only task-owned temporary artifacts,
  obsolete screenshots, builds, or caches. Never broadly clean shared paths or
  delete another task's files. Ask before deleting `node_modules`. Use Mole only
  for user-authorized machine-wide cleanup, never as a workaround for scoped
  repository cleanup.

## Completion report

Keep the final report compact. Include:

- delivered behavior and pushed commit/branch/PR identifiers;
- data-model, migration, type/interface, public API, and important encapsulation
  changes;
- verification performed and where UI evidence lives;
- documentation and handoff updates;
- skills used;
- remaining rough edges, including conventions stretched and why;
- blockers requiring the user, or explicitly state that there are none.

Do not call work complete while an authorized plan item remains actionable.
import * as Schema from 'effect/Schema';
import { ANALYTICS_INSIGHT_TABS, ANALYTICS_TIMEFRAMES, INSIGHT_NOTIFICATION_DEFAULT_TIME } from '@/constants';
import type { CheckIn } from '@/features/check-in/domain/check-in';
import type { BeliefStatement } from '@/features/beliefs/domain/belief-statement';
import { entriesForAnalyticsTimeframe, topLeitsaetzeForTimeframe, AnalyticsTimeframeSchema } from '@/features/analytics/domain/analytics-timeframe';
import { primaryAnalyticsInsights } from '@/features/analytics/domain/check-in-analytics';
import { ReminderLocalTime } from '@/features/reminders/domain/reminder-timing';

export const InsightCandidateSchema = Schema.Struct({
  id: Schema.String.pipe(Schema.minLength(1)),
  timeframe: AnalyticsTimeframeSchema,
  tab: Schema.Literal(ANALYTICS_INSIGHT_TABS.GUIDING_BELIEF, ANALYTICS_INSIGHT_TABS.PATTERN),
  patternId: Schema.NullOr(Schema.String),
});
export type InsightCandidate = typeof InsightCandidateSchema.Type;
export const InsightBatchSchema = Schema.Struct({
  id: Schema.String.pipe(Schema.minLength(1)),
  fireAt: Schema.String,
  candidates: Schema.NonEmptyArray(InsightCandidateSchema),
});
export type InsightBatch = typeof InsightBatchSchema.Type;
export const InsightNotificationStateSchema = Schema.Struct({
  enabled: Schema.Boolean,
  dismissed: Schema.Boolean,
  time: ReminderLocalTime,
  seen: Schema.Array(Schema.String),
  pending: Schema.NullOr(InsightBatchSchema),
});
export type InsightNotificationState = typeof InsightNotificationStateSchema.Type;
export const initialInsightNotificationState = (): InsightNotificationState => ({
  enabled: false, dismissed: false, time: INSIGHT_NOTIFICATION_DEFAULT_TIME, seen: [], pending: null,
});

export function insightCandidates({ entries, statements, now }: {
  entries: readonly CheckIn[]; statements: readonly BeliefStatement[]; now: Date;
}): readonly InsightCandidate[] {
  return Object.values(ANALYTICS_TIMEFRAMES).flatMap((timeframe) => {
    const scoped = entriesForAnalyticsTimeframe({ entries, now, timeframe });
    const group = topLeitsaetzeForTimeframe({ entries, statements, now, timeframe });
    const beliefs = (group?.leitsaetze ?? []).map(({ beliefSystemId }) => ({
      id: `${timeframe}:guiding-belief:${beliefSystemId}`, timeframe,
      tab: ANALYTICS_INSIGHT_TABS.GUIDING_BELIEF, patternId: null,
    }));
    const patterns = primaryAnalyticsInsights(scoped).map((pattern) => {
      const patternId = pattern.kind === 'belief'
        ? `${pattern.kind}:${pattern.emotionId}:${pattern.beliefSystemId}`
        : `${pattern.kind}:${pattern.emotionId}`;
      return { id: `${timeframe}:${patternId}`, timeframe, tab: ANALYTICS_INSIGHT_TABS.PATTERN, patternId };
    });
    return [...beliefs, ...patterns];
  });
}

export function nextInsightDelivery(now: Date, time: typeof ReminderLocalTime.Type) {
  const date = new Date(now);
  date.setHours(time.hour, time.minute, 0, 0);
  if (date <= now) date.setDate(date.getDate() + 1);
  return date;
}

export function pendingInsightCandidates(state: InsightNotificationState, candidates: readonly InsightCandidate[]) {
  const currentIds = new Set(candidates.map(({ id }) => id));
  const pending = state.pending?.candidates.filter(({ id }) => currentIds.has(id)) ?? [];
  const pendingIds = new Set(pending.map(({ id }) => id));
  const additions = candidates.filter(({ id }) => !state.seen.includes(id) && !pendingIds.has(id));
  return [...pending, ...additions];
}
import { AppState, Linking } from 'react-native';
import { INSIGHT_NOTIFICATION_EVENTS, INSIGHT_NOTIFICATION_OWNER, REMINDER_PERMISSION_STATES } from '@/constants';
import type { BeliefStatement } from '@/features/beliefs/domain/belief-statement';
import type { CheckIn } from '@/features/check-in/domain/check-in';
import type { AppLocale } from '@/localization/app-locale';
import type { ReminderLocalTime } from '@/features/reminders/domain/reminder-timing';
import { getReminderPermission, requestReminderPermission } from '@/features/reminders/infrastructure/local-reminder.scheduler';
import { loadInsightNotificationState, persistInsightNotificationState } from '../infrastructure/insight-notification.repository';
import { reconcileInsightBatch, cancelInsightNotifications } from '../infrastructure/insight-notification.scheduler';
import { insightCandidates, nextInsightDelivery, pendingInsightCandidates, type InsightNotificationState } from '../domain/insight-notification';
import { createInsightNotificationStore } from './insight-notification.store';

export type InsightNotificationCommand =
  | { type: typeof INSIGHT_NOTIFICATION_EVENTS.ENABLED }
  | { type: typeof INSIGHT_NOTIFICATION_EVENTS.DISABLED }
  | { type: typeof INSIGHT_NOTIFICATION_EVENTS.DISMISSED }
  | { type: typeof INSIGHT_NOTIFICATION_EVENTS.RECHECK_REQUESTED }
  | { type: typeof INSIGHT_NOTIFICATION_EVENTS.SYSTEM_SETTINGS_REQUESTED }
  | { type: typeof INSIGHT_NOTIFICATION_EVENTS.TIME_CHANGED; time: ReminderLocalTime }
  | { type: typeof INSIGHT_NOTIFICATION_EVENTS.PICKER_CHANGED; open: boolean };
export interface InsightData {
  entries: readonly CheckIn[]; statements: readonly BeliefStatement[]; locale: AppLocale; ready: boolean;
}
export interface InsightDependencies {
  load: typeof loadInsightNotificationState; persist: typeof persistInsightNotificationState;
  permission: typeof getReminderPermission; requestPermission: typeof requestReminderPermission;
  reconcile: typeof reconcileInsightBatch; cancel: typeof cancelInsightNotifications;
  now: () => Date; nonce: () => string; openSettings: () => Promise<void>;
}
export const systemInsightDependencies: InsightDependencies = {
  load: loadInsightNotificationState, persist: persistInsightNotificationState,
  permission: getReminderPermission, requestPermission: requestReminderPermission,
  reconcile: reconcileInsightBatch, cancel: cancelInsightNotifications,
  now: () => new Date(), nonce: () => Math.random().toString(16).slice(2),
  openSettings: () => Linking.openSettings(),
};

export class InsightNotificationCoordinator {
  private queue: Promise<void> = Promise.resolve();
  private loaded = false;
  private resetting = false;
  private data: InsightData | null = null;
  private active = true;
  private readonly store: ReturnType<typeof createInsightNotificationStore>;
  private readonly deps: InsightDependencies;
  constructor(store: ReturnType<typeof createInsightNotificationStore>, deps: InsightDependencies) {
    this.store = store; this.deps = deps;
  }

  private enqueue(task: () => Promise<void>) {
    const run = async () => {
      this.store.trigger.busyChanged({ busy: true });
      try { await task(); }
      catch { this.store.trigger.failed({ message: 'Insight notifications could not be updated. Try again.' }); }
      finally { this.store.trigger.busyChanged({ busy: false }); }
    };
    this.queue = this.queue.then(run);
    return this.queue;
  }
  private async load() {
    if (this.loaded) return;
    const state = await this.deps.load();
    this.store.trigger.updated({ settings: state });
    this.loaded = true;
  }
  private async save(settings: InsightNotificationState) {
    await this.deps.persist(settings);
    this.store.trigger.updated({ settings });
  }
  update(data: InsightData) {
    this.data = data;
    if (!data.ready || !this.active) return this.queue;
    return this.enqueue(async () => { await this.load(); await this.evaluate(); });
  }
  setActive(active: boolean) {
    this.active = active;
    if (active && this.data) return this.update(this.data);
    return this.queue;
  }
  reset() {
    this.resetting = true;
    return this.enqueue(async () => {
      await this.deps.cancel();
      await this.load();
      const state = this.store.getSnapshot().context.settings;
      await this.save({ ...state, pending: null });
    });
  }
  private candidates() {
    if (!this.data?.ready) return [];
    return insightCandidates({ entries: this.data.entries, statements: this.data.statements, now: this.deps.now() });
  }
  private async evaluate() {
    if (!this.data?.ready || !this.active) return;
    let state = this.store.getSnapshot().context.settings;
    const candidates = this.candidates();
    if (this.resetting) {
      await this.save({ ...state, seen: candidates.map(({ id }) => id), pending: null });
      this.resetting = false;
      return;
    }
    const permission = await this.deps.permission();
    this.store.trigger.permissionChanged({ permission });
    if (!state.enabled || permission !== REMINDER_PERMISSION_STATES.GRANTED) {
      await this.deps.cancel();
      return;
    }
    // A due one-shot is consumed; native scheduling does not guarantee receipt.
    if (state.pending && new Date(state.pending.fireAt) <= this.deps.now()) {
      state = { ...state, seen: [...new Set([...state.seen, ...state.pending.candidates.map(({ id }) => id)])], pending: null };
    }
    const pending = pendingInsightCandidates(state, candidates);
    const [first, ...rest] = pending;
    const batch = first ? {
      id: state.pending?.id ?? `${INSIGHT_NOTIFICATION_OWNER}-${this.deps.now().getTime()}-${this.deps.nonce()}`,
      fireAt: state.pending?.fireAt ?? nextInsightDelivery(this.deps.now(), state.time).toISOString(),
      candidates: [first, ...rest] satisfies readonly [typeof first, ...typeof rest],
    } : null;
    // Persist intent before native registration: retry can recover the same request ID.
    await this.save({ ...state, pending: batch });
    await this.deps.reconcile(batch, this.data.locale);
  }
  command(event: InsightNotificationCommand) {
    if (event.type === INSIGHT_NOTIFICATION_EVENTS.PICKER_CHANGED) {
      this.store.trigger.pickerChanged({ open: event.open });
      return this.queue;
    }
    return this.enqueue(async () => { await this.load(); await this.applyCommand(event); });
  }
  private async applyCommand(event: InsightNotificationCommand) {
    const state = this.store.getSnapshot().context.settings;
    if (event.type === INSIGHT_NOTIFICATION_EVENTS.SYSTEM_SETTINGS_REQUESTED) return this.deps.openSettings();
    if (event.type === INSIGHT_NOTIFICATION_EVENTS.RECHECK_REQUESTED) return this.evaluate();
    if (event.type === INSIGHT_NOTIFICATION_EVENTS.DISMISSED) return this.save({ ...state, dismissed: true });
    if (event.type === INSIGHT_NOTIFICATION_EVENTS.DISABLED) {
      await this.deps.cancel();
      return this.save({ ...state, enabled: false, pending: null });
    }
    if (event.type === INSIGHT_NOTIFICATION_EVENTS.TIME_CHANGED) {
      await this.save({ ...state, time: event.time, pending: state.pending
        ? { ...state.pending, fireAt: nextInsightDelivery(this.deps.now(), event.time).toISOString() } : null });
      return this.evaluate();
    }
    if (event.type !== INSIGHT_NOTIFICATION_EVENTS.ENABLED || !this.data?.ready || !this.active) return;
    const permission = await this.deps.requestPermission();
    this.store.trigger.permissionChanged({ permission });
    if (permission !== REMINDER_PERMISSION_STATES.GRANTED) return;
    await this.save({ ...state, enabled: true, dismissed: true, seen: this.candidates().map(({ id }) => id), pending: null });
    await this.evaluate();
  }
}

export function watchInsightAppState(coordinator: InsightNotificationCoordinator) {
  coordinator.setActive(AppState.currentState === 'active');
  return AppState.addEventListener('change', (state) => { void coordinator.setActive(state === 'active'); });
}
import { createStore } from '@xstate/store';
import * as Schema from 'effect/Schema';
import { REMINDER_PERMISSION_STATES } from '@/constants';
import { initialInsightNotificationState, InsightNotificationStateSchema } from '../domain/insight-notification';

const PermissionSchema = Schema.Literal(...Object.values(REMINDER_PERMISSION_STATES));
export function createInsightNotificationStore() {
  return createStore({
    schemas: {
      context: Schema.standardSchemaV1(Schema.Struct({
        settings: InsightNotificationStateSchema, hydrated: Schema.Boolean, busy: Schema.Boolean,
        pickerOpen: Schema.Boolean, permission: PermissionSchema, error: Schema.NullOr(Schema.String),
      })),
      events: {
        updated: Schema.standardSchemaV1(Schema.Struct({ settings: InsightNotificationStateSchema })),
        busyChanged: Schema.standardSchemaV1(Schema.Struct({ busy: Schema.Boolean })),
        permissionChanged: Schema.standardSchemaV1(Schema.Struct({ permission: PermissionSchema })),
        pickerChanged: Schema.standardSchemaV1(Schema.Struct({ open: Schema.Boolean })),
        failed: Schema.standardSchemaV1(Schema.Struct({ message: Schema.String })),
      },
    },
    context: { settings: initialInsightNotificationState(), hydrated: false, busy: false,
      pickerOpen: false, permission: REMINDER_PERMISSION_STATES.UNDETERMINED, error: null },
    on: {
      updated: (context, event) => ({ ...context, settings: event.settings, hydrated: true, error: null }),
      busyChanged: (context, event) => ({ ...context, busy: event.busy }),
      permissionChanged: (context, event) => ({ ...context, permission: event.permission }),
      pickerChanged: (context, event) => ({ ...context, pickerOpen: event.open }),
      failed: (context, event) => ({ ...context, error: event.message }),
    },
  });
}
export const insightNotificationStore = createInsightNotificationStore();
import * as Notifications from 'expo-notifications';
import * as Schema from 'effect/Schema';
import { APP_LOCALES, INSIGHT_NOTIFICATION_OWNER } from '@/constants';
import type { AppLocale } from '@/localization/app-locale';
import { InsightCandidateSchema, type InsightBatch } from '../domain/insight-notification';

export const InsightNotificationPayloadSchema = Schema.Struct({
  owner: Schema.Literal(INSIGHT_NOTIFICATION_OWNER),
  batchId: Schema.String.pipe(Schema.minLength(1)),
  target: InsightCandidateSchema,
});
export async function cancelInsightNotifications() {
  const requests = await Notifications.getAllScheduledNotificationsAsync();
  await Promise.all(requests.filter(({ content }) => content.data?.['owner'] === INSIGHT_NOTIFICATION_OWNER)
    .map(({ identifier }) => Notifications.cancelScheduledNotificationAsync(identifier)));
}
export async function reconcileInsightBatch(batch: InsightBatch | null, locale: AppLocale) {
  const requests = await Notifications.getAllScheduledNotificationsAsync();
  const own = requests.filter(({ content }) => content.data?.['owner'] === INSIGHT_NOTIFICATION_OWNER);
  const expected = batch ? Schema.encodeSync(Schema.parseJson(Schema.Struct({
    batch: Schema.String, fireAt: Schema.String, locale: Schema.String,
    candidates: Schema.Array(InsightCandidateSchema),
  })))({ batch: batch.id, fireAt: batch.fireAt, locale, candidates: batch.candidates }) : '';
  const matching = own.find(({ identifier, content }) => identifier === batch?.id && content.data?.['fingerprint'] === expected);
  for (const request of own) {
    if (request !== matching) await Notifications.cancelScheduledNotificationAsync(request.identifier);
  }
  if (!batch || matching) return;
  const target = batch.candidates[0];
  if (!target) return;
  await Notifications.scheduleNotificationAsync({
    identifier: batch.id,
    content: {
      title: locale === APP_LOCALES.GERMAN ? 'Ein neuer Einblick ist da' : 'A new insight is ready',
      body: locale === APP_LOCALES.GERMAN ? 'Öffne Youmotion, um deinen Einblick anzusehen.' : 'Open Youmotion to see your insight.',
      sound: false,
      data: { owner: INSIGHT_NOTIFICATION_OWNER, batchId: batch.id, target, fingerprint: expected },
    },
    trigger: { type: Notifications.SchedulableTriggerInputTypes.DATE, date: new Date(batch.fireAt) },
  });
}
import AsyncStorage from '@react-native-async-storage/async-storage';
import * as Schema from 'effect/Schema';
import * as Effect from 'effect/Effect';
import { INSIGHT_NOTIFICATION_STORAGE_KEY } from '@/constants';
import { InsightNotificationStateSchema, initialInsightNotificationState, type InsightNotificationState } from '../domain/insight-notification';

export class InsightNotificationStorageError extends Schema.TaggedError<InsightNotificationStorageError>()(
  'InsightNotificationStorageError', { cause: Schema.Defect },
) {}
const StoredStateSchema = Schema.parseJson(InsightNotificationStateSchema);
export async function loadInsightNotificationState() {
  return Effect.runPromise(Effect.tryPromise({
    try: () => AsyncStorage.getItem(INSIGHT_NOTIFICATION_STORAGE_KEY),
    catch: (cause) => InsightNotificationStorageError.make({ cause }),
  }).pipe(Effect.flatMap((value) => value === null
    ? Effect.succeed(initialInsightNotificationState())
    : Schema.decode(StoredStateSchema)(value))));
}
export async function persistInsightNotificationState(state: InsightNotificationState) {
  const encoded = await Effect.runPromise(Schema.encode(StoredStateSchema)(state));
  return Effect.runPromise(Effect.tryPromise({
    try: () => AsyncStorage.setItem(INSIGHT_NOTIFICATION_STORAGE_KEY, encoded),
    catch: (cause) => InsightNotificationStorageError.make({ cause }),
  }));
}

